Z||000034||Tryxalon||11-24-2000||08:46 PM||||I'm 6'0" 240 lbs. <P>While getting in and out might be difficult for the inflexible, once in the car it is larger and more comfortable than anything I have driven other than an 60's Caddy CDV. <P>And while there is a trick of "falling in" and a "crouch, twist, stand" exit, it is easier to get in and out than most sportscars.  <P>I fit perfectly with the seat 12 clicks forward from the rear stop. That puts clutch, brake, accellerator, shift, wheel and most other controls perfectly in place.<P> I do slide the seat all the way back and tilt the wheel away on enter/exit. <P>  ||||reg||1
