Z||000068||Sndfr||12-02-2000||05:11 PM||||I'm 6'2 199 lbs. of buffscular manlyness.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I almost didn't buy my first fiero.  I went to the viewing very skeptical about interior room.  I got in to test drive it and almost decided not to, but it was such a good price and i needed a car ($650, i straight-up STOLE that thing for how damn good condition it's in).  So off i go and then i have a brain storm.  Push the seat back!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>Wow.  All my friends love how comfortable it is 'cause of the compact space.  Plus it has brand new seats.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>The funniest thing though is my old-school best friend comes down from Sacramento State College for holidays.  He's a starting lineman, tipping the scales at 6'7, 280 pounds of lean muscle.  Even <I>he</I> fits perfectly except one thing... he needs two more inches of head room......<P>...so i put the sunroof up!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>-<B>matthew "Whyt Nyte" d.</B><BR>84 SE<BR><I>"You are not special.<BR>You are not a beatiful and unique snowflake.<BR>You are the same decaying organic matter as everyone else."</I>||||reg||6
